1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"phase-x--xx-optional-proficiency-testing","kind":"phase-article","route":"/roadmap/phase-x/xx-optional-proficiency-testing","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/phase-x/xx-optional-proficiency-testing","sourceHash":"2aabf1cd695a10cf10462e1efe15ced67dee6c7e84214f1f70e436601f5cfcf4","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T23:12:12.701Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"XX (Optional) — Proficiency Testing","zh":"XX（可选）——能力测试"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"what-youre-doing","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"What You're Doing","zh":"你正在做什么"}},{"id":"segment-0002","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Many learners want or need a formal certification of their language ability — for university admission, immigration, job applications, or personal satisfaction. This optional sub-phase is about preparing for and passing a standardized language proficiency test (CEFR, JLPT, HSK, DELE, DELF, TOPIK, etc.).","zh":"许多学习者希望或需要获得语言能力的正式认证——用于大学录取、移民、求职，或满足个人成就感。这个可选子阶段旨在准备并通过标准化语言能力考试（CEFR、JLPT、HSK、DELE、DELF、TOPIK等）。"}},{"id":"segment-0003","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The good news: if you've been following the Refold method, you have a massive advantage over traditional test-takers. Your comprehension, vocabulary, and intuitive feel for the language are far ahead of what most classroom learners achieve.","zh":"好消息是：如果你一直遵循Refold方法，你相比传统应试者拥有巨大优势。你的理解能力、词汇量和对语言的直觉感，已经远远超过大多数课堂学习者所能达到的水平。"}},{"id":"segment-0004","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The challenge is that proficiency tests have specific formats, question types, and expectations that you may not be familiar with.","zh":"挑战在于，能力测试有特定的格式、题型和要求，而你可能并不熟悉。"}},{"id":"segment-0005","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"This sub-phase can be done at any point from Phase 4 onward, depending on which level you're aiming for. The key is to combine your genuine language ability with targeted test preparation.","zh":"根据你所瞄准的等级，这个子阶段可以从第4阶段开始后的任何时间进行。关键是将你真实的语言能力与针对性的考试准备结合起来。"}},{"id":"segment-0006","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"If you need to do it before reading Phase 4, you can still use the recommendations, but you'll need to implement output practice (if your targeted test requires it). You can skip ahead in the Phases to see the recommended activities.","zh":"如果你需要在阅读第4阶段之前参加考试，仍然可以使用这些建议，但你需要进行输出练习（如果目标考试要求输出）。你可以跳到后面的阶段，查看推荐的活动。"}},{"id":"whats-new","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"What's New","zh":"新增内容"}},{"id":"segment-0008","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Test Prep</strong> — Get a guided course or prep book for the specific test and level you're targeting. Learn the format: how many sections, what types of questions, time limits, scoring. Practice the specific sections that will be on the test and score your own attempts to understand what, specifically, to improve for the next time.","zh":"<strong>考试准备</strong>——针对你要参加的具体考试和等级，找一套有指导性的课程或备考书。了解考试格式：有多少部分、有哪些题型、时间限制和评分方式。练习考试中会出现的具体部分，并给自己的作答评分，以明确下一次需要改进的地方。"}},{"id":"segment-0009","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Take <em>at least</em> 2 practice tests, with at least 1 under exact exam conditions (timed, no dictionary, no breaks outside what the test allows). <a href=\"/roadmap/library/proficiency-testing\">Proficiency Testing</a>","zh":"至少参加<em>2</em>次模拟考试，其中至少1次要在完全相同的考试条件下进行（计时、不使用词典、除考试允许的休息外不休息）。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/proficiency-testing\">能力测试</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0010","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Grammar Study (test-focused)</strong> — Proficiency tests often test grammar points that come up less frequently in natural immersion — rare conjugations, formal writing patterns, and fine distinctions that native speakers don't think about consciously (or make in the spoken language). Targeted grammar study focused on what the test actually tests is essential. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/grammar-study\">Grammar Study</a>","zh":"<strong>语法学习（以考试为重点）</strong>——能力测试经常考查一些在自然沉浸中较少出现的语法点——罕见的变形、正式书面语模式，以及母语者不会有意识思考（或在口语中使用）的细微区别。针对考试实际考查内容进行语法学习至关重要。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/grammar-study\">语法学习</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0011","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Writing practice (test format)</strong> — Most proficiency tests include a writing section with specific requirements (word count, topic type, structure). Practice writing in the exact format the test expects. If the test requires a formal letter, practice formal letters. If it requires an argumentative essay, practice argumentative essays. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/assisted-writing\">Assisted Writing</a>","zh":"<strong>写作练习（考试格式）</strong>——大多数能力测试都包含写作部分，并有具体要求（字数、主题类型、结构）。按照考试要求的确切格式练习写作。如果考试要求写正式信函，就练习正式信函；如果要求写议论文，就练习议论文。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/assisted-writing\">辅助写作</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0012","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"If your test requires handwriting (which many still do), make sure you practice that! If your writing is illegible or you take too long to write, it might reduce your test score for no good reason. <a href=\"https://refold.la/learning-libraries?item=40203-handwriting-practice&amp;type=activity\">-&gt; Handwriting Practice</a>","zh":"如果你的考试要求手写（许多考试仍然如此），一定要练习！如果你的字迹难以辨认，或者写得太慢，可能会在没有正当理由的情况下影响考试分数。<a href=\"https://refold.la/learning-libraries?item=40203-handwriting-practice&amp;type=activity\">-&gt; 手写练习</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0013","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Speaking practice (test format)</strong> — If the test includes a speaking section, practice with the specific format: timed responses, structured prompts, and formal register. This is often quite different from casual conversation. Look for a tutor who has experience with the test you want to take. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/speaking-with-partner\">Speaking with Partner</a>","zh":"<strong>口语练习（考试格式）</strong>——如果考试包含口语部分，请按照具体格式进行练习：限时回答、结构化提示和正式语体。这通常与日常对话有很大不同。找一位有你目标考试经验的辅导老师。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/speaking-with-partner\">与伙伴练习口语</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0014","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Since tests naturally require strict grading procedures to ensure fairness, speaking tests are often more rigid than you might expect. Examiners can't just go off of vibes, so they're looking for specific criteria. If you can give them exactly what they want, you'll get a very good score.","zh":"由于考试自然需要严格的评分程序来确保公平，口语考试通常比你想象的更加僵化。考官不能只凭感觉评分，因此他们会寻找具体标准。如果你能准确提供他们想要的内容，就能取得很好的分数。"}},{"id":"your-routine","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Your Routine","zh":"你的日常安排"}},{"id":"segment-0016","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Balanced across all skills, with a focus on weak areas: <a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-pillars-of-language-learning\">The Pillars of Language Learning</a>","zh":"均衡覆盖所有技能，同时重点加强薄弱环节：<a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-pillars-of-language-learning\">语言学习的支柱</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0017","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"<strong>Priming:</strong> 25%","zh":"<strong>预热：</strong>25%"},{"en":"<strong>Interactive Immersion:</strong> 25%","zh":"<strong>互动式沉浸：</strong>25%"},{"en":"<strong>Freeflow Immersion:</strong> 25%","zh":"<strong>自由流沉浸：</strong>25%"},{"en":"<strong>Output:</strong> 25%","zh":"<strong>输出：</strong>25%"}]},{"id":"sample-daily-schedule","type":"heading","level":3,"content":{"en":"Sample Daily Schedule","zh":"每日安排示例"}},{"id":"segment-0019","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Test Prep: 30 mins","zh":"考试准备：30分钟"},{"en":"Interactive Reading: 30 mins","zh":"互动式阅读：30分钟"},{"en":"Freeflow Listening: 30 mins","zh":"自由流听力：30分钟"},{"en":"Speaking with Partner or Unassisted Writing: 30 mins","zh":"与伙伴练习口语或无辅助写作：30分钟"}]},{"id":"when-are-you-done","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"When Are You Done?","zh":"什么时候算完成？"}},{"id":"segment-0021","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"You're done when you've passed your desired test. Good luck!","zh":"当你通过目标考试时，就算完成。祝你好运！"}}],"cards":[]}}]
